9
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
The Accused is a 1988 American legal drama film directed by Jonathan Kaplan and written by Tom Topor,
loosely based on the 1983 gang rape of Cheryl Araujo in New Bedford, Massachusetts.

10
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
It stars Jodie Foster as Sarah Tobias, a young waitress who
is gang raped by three men at a local bar.

11
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:30,000
With the help of Deputy District Attorney Katheryn Murphy (played by Kelly McGillis), she
sets out to prosecute the rapists and the men who helped induce the assault.

12
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
The Accused was released in limited theaters in North America on October 14, 1988, and premiered the following
year at the 39th Berlin International Film Festival, where it competed for the Golden Bear.

13
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:18,000
The film was highly controversial upon release due to
its graphic portrayal of gang rape.

14
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
Despite this, it received widespread acclaim from critics, with many praising the
performances of the cast and authentic portrayal of its subject matter.

15
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
It was chosen by the National Board of Review as the 3rd-best film of the year.

16
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:30,000
It was credited as one of the first mainstream films to deal with the
horrors of rape and its aftermath on a victim's life.

17
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:54,000
Foster's performance marked her breakthrough into adult roles, earning numerous
accolades including the Academy Award for Best Actress at the 61st ceremony.

18
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
The film explores themes of mistaken identity, revenge,
false accusations, home invasion, doxxing.

19
01:23:36,000 --> 01:23:42,000
The tone is emotional and intense.
